      {
        "id": 211293,
        "name": "Nilus",
        "username": "Nilus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nilus/{size}/2099_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-12-21T19:09:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Blackfang108\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/74df32/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Blackfang108:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Powerhound_2000 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>I’m sure it’ll come back.&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nDear sweet entropy, I hope not.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Dear Lord of Order, &nbsp;let this joke be reborn!</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Seriosuoy don’t get why it gets so much hate. It’s silly and stupid but not like it eats up 90% of the episode. &nbsp; I know some people really don’t like all the metajoke questions from the likes of the Cult of Gloom and such but I think the podcast would be a lot less entertaining without it&nbsp;</p>",
