      {
        "id": 211295,
        "name": "Blackfang108",
        "username": "Blackfang108",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/74df32/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-12-21T19:58:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Nilus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nilus/48/2099_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Nilus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Blackfang108 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;Powerhound_2000 wrote:<br><blockquote>I’m sure it’ll come back.&nbsp;&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nDear sweet entropy, I hope not.\n</blockquote></div>\nDear Lord of Order, &nbsp;let this joke be reborn!&nbsp;Seriosuoy don’t get why it gets so much hate. It’s silly and stupid but not like it eats up 90% of the episode. &nbsp; I know some people really don’t like all the metajoke questions from the likes of the Cult of Gloom and such but I think the podcast would be a lot less entertaining without it&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>And the Metajoke stuff hit its peak&nbsp;when someone sent in a letter with an entire page of \"not related to&nbsp;SotM metagag\" preceeding the actual question.</p>\n<p>The \"OMG, can't say a name\" was slightly amusing at first (and yes, IHIP and Lennys still are), but the \"Smoctor Schmoo\" shenanagins often makes it hard to tell what they're even referring to.&nbsp; And it's a little jarring, because there's no actual reason for it.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:41:49.850Z",
